 Experience performing project vessel mobilizations and demobilizations;
 Offshore field experience related to the installation and decommissioning of subsea infrastructure;
 Knowledge of specialized software would be an asset (Example- Ansys/Inventor- Structural/Mechanical Engineers, Orcaflex- Hydrodynamics- Subsea Engineers, etc.);
 Knowledge of the marine environment and technical challenges associated with executing projects in these conditions;
 Knowledge of subsea infrastructure components, deployment/recovery methodologies, equipment handling restrictions, testing requirements, etc.;
 Knowledge of DNV lifting and underwater deployment/recovery codes pertaining to marine operations;
 Analytical and technical capabilities specific to lowering analyses and rigging design would be an asset;
 General technical knowledge of sea fastening design and analysis (vessel motions & structural design);
 General knowledge of industry and regulatory standards, best practices, and design codes;
 Excellent working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite;
 Excellent technical writing and verbal communication skills;
 Willingness to perform the work required to complete the project on time while meeting client expectations;
 Willingness to share experiences and teach critical skills/tasks to other team members;
 Professional demeanor to promote company interests expected always.
 (Training programme can compensate for lack of experience.)
